flowchart TD
    box_0(["Start"])
    box_1["Complete the following checks: 1. Check the coolant<br/>level against the tank minimum and maximum marks. 2.<br/>Assess coolant colour and odour for signs of<br/>contamination. 3. Check refractometer reading<br/>against the specified concentration range."]
    box_2{"Severe contamination: tramp oil, biological growth<br/>or discolouration?"}
    box_3(["End, Drain and replace coolant: severe<br/>contamination, hazardous substance disposal"])
    box_4["Draw a 10 millilitre sample of coolant from the sump<br/>using a clean pipette and place two drops on the<br/>refractometer prism. Close the cover and read the<br/>coolant concentration from the refractometer scale<br/>under a light source. Multiply the reading by the<br/>specific correction factor for this coolant brand<br/>and compare the calculated concentration against the<br/>target range in the coolant specification."]
    box_5[/"Refer to the coolant concentration specification."/]
    box_6{"Concentration within specified Brix range?"}
    box_7["Top up with concentrate or deionised water to<br/>correct concentration"]
    box_8{"Reverify concentration after top up"}
    box_9(["End, Escalate: concentration drift rate excessive,<br/>check mixing system"])
    box_10["Immerse the calibrated pH meter probe in the coolant<br/>sump to a depth of at least 50 millimetres and wait<br/>for the reading to stabilise for 30 seconds. Record<br/>the pH value. Coolant pH below 8.5 indicates<br/>accelerated corrosion risk; above 9.5 indicates risk<br/>of skin sensitisation and requires immediate<br/>corrective dilution or biocide treatment."]
    box_11[/"Refer to the coolant pH specification."/]
    box_12{"pH within acceptable range?"}
    box_13["Add pH correction agent per dosing table"]
    box_14["Read the inline flow meter display with the coolant<br/>pump running at normal operating speed. Record the<br/>flow rate in litres per minute and compare against<br/>the minimum required flow rate for the machine<br/>specification. If no inline meter is fitted, use the<br/>timed bucket method at the main return line and<br/>calculate flow rate from volume and elapsed time."]
    box_15[/"Refer to the coolant flow rate specification."/]
    box_16{"Coolant flow rate within specified range?"}
    box_17["Replace coolant filter element and clean strainer<br/>basket"]
    box_18{"Reverify flow rate after filter replacement"}
    box_19(["End, Escalate: pump cavitation or blockage suspected"])
    box_20["Immerse a calibrated thermocouple probe or a<br/>calibrated thermometer in the main coolant return<br/>line at the sump entry point after the machine has<br/>been running under cutting load for at least 15<br/>minutes. Record the coolant temperature and compare<br/>against the maximum permitted sump temperature in<br/>the machine specification; temperatures above 35<br/>degrees Celsius degrade coolant life and reduce<br/>cutting performance."]
    box_21{"Coolant return temperature within operating range?"}
    box_22["Complete the following checks: 1. Inspect the heat<br/>exchanger coil surfaces for dust or scale deposits.<br/>2. Check the coolant pump outlet pressure against<br/>the rated value. 3. Verify all coolant nozzles are<br/>unobstructed and correctly directed."]
    box_23["Shut off coolant flow and remove each nozzle from<br/>the manifold. Hold each nozzle against a light<br/>source and inspect the orifice for swarf blockage or<br/>mineral deposits. Blocked nozzles should be soaked<br/>in descaler for 10 minutes then cleared with a wire<br/>of the correct gauge. Replace nozzles where the<br/>orifice shows erosion or enlargement beyond the<br/>nominal drill size."]
    box_24{"All coolant nozzles unobstructed and correctly<br/>directed?"}
    box_25["Unblock or replace blocked coolant nozzles"]
    box_26["With the coolant pump running, observe the chip<br/>conveyor return flow inlet at the sump end. Coolant<br/>should be flowing visibly back to the sump through<br/>the return channel. Absence of return flow indicates<br/>a blocked return strainer or a conveyor drive fault;<br/>check the return strainer basket and clear any<br/>accumulated chip material."]
    box_27{"Coolant recovery from chip conveyor operating<br/>correctly?"}
    box_28["Clear chip conveyor return tray and check drain<br/>ports"]
    box_29["Use a clean dipstick or graduated probe to measure<br/>the depth of settled sediment at three points in the<br/>sump: near the pump inlet, at the centre, and at the<br/>far end from the pump. Record the maximum reading<br/>and compare against the maximum permitted sediment<br/>depth in the sump cleaning schedule. Sediment<br/>exceeding 25 millimetres requires immediate sump<br/>pump out and cleaning."]
    box_30{"Sump sediment depth below 20 mm?"}
    box_31["Schedule sump clean, drain, scrub and refill"]
    box_32["System function test, run machine cycle, verify<br/>coolant delivery"]
    box_33["Log coolant data, refractometer reading and update<br/>service record"]
    box_34(["End, Procedure complete"])
    box_35["Secondary coolant correction: drain 20% of the sump<br/>volume using the sump pump and discard the drained<br/>coolant. Refill the sump with clean water to the<br/>previous level, then add the calculated volume of<br/>coolant concentrate to reach the target<br/>concentration. Run the circulation pump for 5<br/>minutes to mix thoroughly before returning to the<br/>refractometer concentration measurement step."]

